  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-5TO10-R5-027$qb$, $qb$A2-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$The conclusion may influence resource allocation, so alternative explanations need to be tested. How does a critical thinker objectively evaluate vendor claims regarding software efficiency gains?$qb$, $qb$Scrutinizing raw performance data, assessing workflow compatibility, and requesting structured trials.$qb$, $qb$Presenting vendor claims to leadership, highlighting positive client testimonials and advertised benefits.$qb$, $qb$Requesting vendor pricing discounts before deciding whether to pilot the software tool.$qb$, $qb$Consulting other internal departments to inquire if they have utilized similar vendor tools in past projects.$qb$, $qb$Accepting vendor statistics as valid industry benchmarks and recommending software adoption.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-5TO10-R5-028$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Several local fixes have already treated symptoms without preventing recurrence. What is the most effective approach to identify root causes when service satisfaction scores decline?$qb$, $qb$Deconstructing ticket lifecycle metrics, mapping processing stages, and testing targeted workflow fixes.$qb$, $qb$Holding brainstorming sessions with service agents to gather qualitative opinions on service delays.$qb$, $qb$Establishing daily ticket processing quotas for agents to raise overall operational speed.$qb$, $qb$Escalating satisfaction drops to leadership with recommendations for temporary staffing additions.$qb$, $qb$Sending follow-up survey forms to dissatisfied customers to collect additional individual complaints.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
