  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-25PLUS-R02-028$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$The organization repeatedly experiences 'unexpected' capacity crises even though each one has a different local trigger. What should leadership investigate?$qb$, $qb$Look for common portfolio assumptions, buffers, incentives, information delays and resource-allocation structures that make the system fragile to different triggers.$qb$, $qb$Address the largest immediate risk and defer less visible enterprise consequences until the next planning cycle.$qb$, $qb$Run a bounded pilot but leave success criteria and the next decision threshold undefined.$qb$, $qb$Ask relevant operating leaders to absorb the issue within existing authority and resources.$qb$, $qb$Choose the option that best protects current reported performance and reputation.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
